1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,020
We have to find Joey before it's too late!

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:10,064
That chump's gonna have to wait,
cause we've got bigger problems!

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,150
Huh?

5
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:12,063
That's not good.

6
00:00:12,146 --> 00:00:13,020
We're surrounded!

7
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,540
Here we are, old chump!

8
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:17,720
Glad you could make it.

9
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,660
Now let's get down to business, shall we?

10
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,700
Look, pal, I want Mai back!

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,471
I led you here to get rid of you for good!

12
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:28,217
Cause Mai can't be happy with you around!

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,712
It's time for me to teach you
a lesson Joey Wheeler style.

14
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:35,537
You're going to be sorry you've
ever messed with my friends.

15
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:36,450
Then let's go.

16
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:40,180
Wait till you see what my
deck of armor can really do.

17
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,582
Ha ha ha ha ha!

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,380
You're on the move!

19
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,120
It's time to duel!

20
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,380
They're closing in.

21
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,420
Maybe we can outrun them.

22
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,960
I already tried that.

23
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:55,160
They're too fast.

24
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,940
Yugi, wait.

25
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:00,420
Seto, it's too dangerous.

26
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:04,420
There's nothing dangerous
about a bunch of holograms.

27
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,480
Now let's shut them down.

28
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,040
Kaiba, look!

29
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,380
Our dragons!

30
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,340
Tobias, come forth!

31
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:25,880
I play Fang of Critias!

32
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,978
You're putting me to sleep, Wheeler.

33
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,492
Hurry up and make a move so I
can continue to torture you.

34
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,557
You're the one that's going
to be in a world of hurt.

35
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,470
Got that?

36
00:02:46,553 --> 00:02:48,481
And it all starts with this card!

37
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,060
My Marauding Captain!

38
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:52,720
And I'm playing him in attack mode!

39
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:56,770
Next,

40
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,417
thanks to my captain's special ability
I get to summon another monster

41
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:06,820
to the field And I choose this bad
boy My battle warrior in attack mode

42
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,200
First I'll use my marauding captain

43
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,677
Attack!

44
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,600
Target his life points

45
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:24,000
And now, battle warrior, it's your turn

46
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,020
How about that?

47
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,900
It'll take more than that
to keep me down Yeah, huh?

48
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:39,340
It's not the minor leagues,
mate This duel's for real

49
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,420
What's this guy so confident about?

50
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:45,407
He doesn't even have
one monster on the field

51
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,817
You think you can do any better?

52
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,260
Take your best shot.

53
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,820
If you say so.

54
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:57,890
What?

55
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,857
That helmet thing already
went to the graveyard.

56
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:03,377
Haven't you ever heard
of a special ability?

57
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:05,857
When psychic armor head's in my graveyard,

58
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:08,705
I can automatically bring
it back to the field.

59
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:09,860
Too bad, chum.

60
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:12,997
But my psychic armor
head should be the least

61
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,557
of your worries if you
know what I'm getting at.

62
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,640
No, not that!

63
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,880
Well, looks like you're
starting to catch on, mate.

64
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,980
I play the seal of Ori Kulkos!

65
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,400
Oh, no!

66
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:41,697
Someone's activating the sacred seal,
and I have a feeling I know who.

67
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:45,640
And that loser better leave
a piece of Wheeler for me.

68
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,840
It's showtime!

69
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:11,640
Now my armor head gets a nice power boost!

70
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:18,320
Then I'll activate the magic
card, Full Armour Gravitation.

71
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:21,957
This little number lets me
draw ten cards from my deck,

72
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:25,628
and if any are armour cards, I
get to summon them right away.

73
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,760
More armour cards?

74
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,580
First I'll summon Burning Knuckle.

75
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,720
Then I'll play Jet Gauntlet.

76
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:41,220
After that, it's Overboost, Active Guard,

77
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:47,917
buster knuckle and advanced
shield let me guess you're putting

78
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,700
on another funky space suit
you're smaller than you look

79
00:05:55,960 --> 00:06:00,372
last time he strapped on that armor he
blew away almost half my life points

80
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,840
I'M INVINCIBLE!

81
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,577
Opponent's life points, 2100.

82
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,477
Marauding captain, strength, 1200.

83
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,325
Battle warrior, strength, 700.

84
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,980
Are you gonna attack or what?

85
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:37,900
Why are you in such a rush?

86
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:41,336
This suit of armor is even
stronger than the last one!

87
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:45,920
But each piece of his little
costume only has 500 attack points.

88
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,960
It's time to calculate your demise.

89
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:51,937
Target identified.

90
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:54,300
Suggested offense, Buster Knuckle.

91
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:58,000
Probability of success, 99%.

92
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,240
Hey, what did you do?

93
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:08,897
Buster Knuckle gets 200 attack points
for every armor card I have on the field.

94
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:10,800
For a grand total of 1,900.

95
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:20,457
too much for you is it
not even close i've been

96
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,797
through much worse we're
just getting started by

97
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,957
the end of this duel
you'll be begging for mercy

98
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,737
then your old buddy mind
will see what a pathetic

99
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,477
chunk you really are and
hopefully she'll realize

100
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,577
why she walked out at
you in the first place

101
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:37,777
so she can move on
already watch it look mate

102
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:40,860
all i'm watching out for
is myself And right now,

103
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,377
the best thing for me
is to get rid of you.

104
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:48,048
Because as long as you're around, Mai's
going to be obsessed with dueling you.

105
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,210
That's right.

106
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:52,617
Since your last duel, all
she talks about is a rematch.

107
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:56,288
But I can't let Mai put herself
in that kind of danger again.

108
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,900
So I got to you first.

109
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:03,740
You see, Wheeler, I'm not such a bad guy.

110
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,687
We both want the same thing.

111
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,340
We want Mai to be happy.

112
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,400
Come on, get real.

113
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,900
If you really wanted Mai to be happy,

114
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,477
you wouldn't have brainwashed
her in the first place.

115
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:19,280
I told you, she chose to join us! No way!

116
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:23,277
I know Mai, and she never would
have walked out on us like that.

117
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,577
Not unless someone messed with her head.

118
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:29,660
And if you ask me, this darts guy
is messing with all of your heads.

119
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:34,100
That Ori Kalkos card he gave
you has evil magic in it.

120
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,809
And it makes everyone
who holds it go nuts.

121
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:38,780
Are you done?

122
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,064
If you are, then allow
me to tell you the truth.

123
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:45,817
That Ori Kulkhouse car did more
for mine than you ever could.

124
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,120
She was weak, and it made her strong.

125
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,540
She was lost, and it showed her the way.

126
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:56,655
Welcome to our family, Miss Valentine.

127
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:11,260
Now go, and remember the
Aurichalcos is always with you.

128
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:18,020
So, how does it feel?

129
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:20,436
You've got what you've always wanted.

130
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,380
Look, I appreciate you taking me here,

131
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:27,900
but don't think this means
I owe you anything. What?

132
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:33,777
I do things my way, and I have no interest
in being part of some team, Valon.

133
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:37,566
I already made that mistake once,
and you know where it got me?

134
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:39,060
Absolutely nowhere.

135
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:41,100
So no thanks.

136
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,120
I know what you mean.

137
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,831
You and I are exactly the same, Valentine.

138
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,820
We're both loners.

139
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:53,015
But you have to admit,
sometimes it's not all that fun.

140
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,800
Why the long face, Mai?

141
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:03,777
You just accomplished your first
mission with flying colors.

142
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:04,690
Yeah, I know.

143
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:08,480
But defeating Pegasus
meant nothing to me. Eh?

144
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:12,940
There's only one person out
there I need to take apart,

145
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,020
and that chump's Joey Wheeler.

146
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:19,700
I can't stand the sight of
you, and neither can I, mate.

147
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:22,540
So I plan to take you down for her.

148
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:27,700
Once you're out of the picture, she can
move on to bigger and much better things.

149
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:32,140
Like teaming up with me and leaving
behind her past once and for all.

150
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:33,610
No way.

151
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,417
Mai would never want to get rid of
me after what we've been through.

152
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,330
We're friends!

153
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,800
Get up off the floor, Joey.

154
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:43,500
And quit all your crying already.

155
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,160
You look like a big baby.

156
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:46,820
Who's crying?

157
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,669
I got something in my eye.

158
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:50,817
Stupid thing won't come out.

159
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:51,730
Here.

160
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,700
Just don't go blowing your nose in it.

161
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:58,600
And by the way, good luck out there today.

162
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,340
It's the card I needed.

163
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,720
Mai has nothing in common with you.

164
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:10,177
So she may be a little
rough around the edges,

165
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:12,597
and she can't have an attitude
every once in a while.

166
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:15,397
But she'd never join up
with a bunch of lowlives

167
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:18,297
who have some crazy plan
to take over the world.

168
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:19,440
We'll just see.

169
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:24,380
Whatever you guys did to her, I'm
gonna undo as soon as I win this.

170
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:26,300
So why don't we move on?

171
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:28,610
Yes!

172
00:11:28,693 --> 00:11:33,720
I sacrificed my battle warrior so
I can summon Jinzo to the field.

173
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:40,780
Jinzo detective, attack strength, 2400.

174
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:43,340
Special ability, destroys traps.

175
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,680
Jinzo, attack now!

176
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,800
Crush his psychic arm ahead!

177
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,320
Initiating attack deflection.

178
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,530
Hey,

179
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:06,060
I attacked your helmet,
not that thing No kidding,

180
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:08,457
but whenever a piece
of my armor is attacked

181
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:12,540
I can redirect the blast
to another piece So,

182
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:18,220
you can hide inside your tin can, but you
can't destroy Jinzo I have to disagree,

183
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,340
my armor's full of surprises

184
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,960
Oh, man, we're goners.

185
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,080
Tobias, attack!

186
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:40,800
Are you two all right?

187
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,720
We are now.

188
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:43,980
Thanks, Yugi.

189
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,420
You did it, bro!

190
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,120
That's all of them!

191
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:04,300
That was a close one Where were you two?

192
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:10,740
Uh, we tried to lead those things away
Yeah, by running really far Hey, wait up!

193
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,550
Kaiba, stop!

194
00:13:12,633 --> 00:13:14,580
We have to stick together

195
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:19,612
Do you geeks think that just cuz I
helped you fight off some holograms now?

196
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,417
I'm part of your little pep squad.

197
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,760
I'm afraid you got the wrong idea

198
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:27,200
Adios, it's been a real blast

199
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:31,127
Kyber will you at least
help us to find Joey?

200
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,760
Use your heads

201
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:38,007
There's a simple way to find
that loser if you think about it.

202
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:41,460
What a sweetheart Wait! Of course!

203
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,660
Joey's dual disc is activated,

204
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:47,841
so we track down his location with
the Kaiba Corp satellite system.

205
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:49,870
Kaiba!

206
00:13:49,953 --> 00:13:52,822
We need to access your
company's tracking system!

207
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,020
Come back!

208
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:59,360
I know you can still hear us!
Whatever. Just let him go.

209
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:03,700
I hacked into his system
once, and I'll do it again.

210
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:20,417
What are we going to do if Rebecca can't
crack the code and track down Joey?

211
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,437
We'll cross that bridge when we get there.

212
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:25,285
We just got to have a
little faith, that's all.

213
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,160
My move, Wheeler!

214
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:34,840
Now, the fun continues.

215
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:39,279
Target identified.

216
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:42,200
Suggested offense, Burning Knuckle.

217
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:47,220
Your attack points just went up again.

218
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:49,480
Let me guess. Yep,

219
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,197
just like Buster Knuckle,

220
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:55,633
this card gets an extra 200 attack
points for every armor monster in play.

221
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,155
Well, it's still weaker than my Jinzo.

222
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,280
You'll never learn.

223
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,540
Watch this.

224
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,080
He's lost it.

225
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:08,180
I'm attacking your Jinzo with
Burning Knuckle. Cheerio.

226
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,140
Nice try.

227
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:24,911
But your metal arm was no match for Jinzo.

228
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:27,060
What's so funny?

229
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,740
Take a closer look, mate.

230
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,560
Your Jinzo's seen better days.

231
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:34,999
How'd you do that?

232
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,837
He lost almost all his points.

233
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,332
Burning Knuckles got a nasty side effect.

234
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:43,795
When it's destroyed, its attack points
get subtracted from your monster.

235
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,150
Yeah,

236
00:15:45,233 --> 00:15:46,917
but you still have to
give up almost half your

237
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,824
life points just to lower
my monster's strength.

238
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,380
He just took a really big risk.

239
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,317
This guy must have a lot
of faith in that armor

240
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,165
of his to willingly let
go of all those points.

241
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,496
Either that or he's just really dumb.

242
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,288
It looks like you're
out of luck, tough guy.

243
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:08,480
I summon Rocket Warrior in attack mode.

244
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:14,620
Rocket Warrior, attack his overboost!

245
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:19,126
Initiating attack deflection.

246
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:27,140
Oh well, there goes your shield.

247
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:30,217
But my Rocket Warrior comes
away without a scratch,

248
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:32,857
because I was smart enough to
put him in invincible mode.

249
00:16:32,940 --> 00:16:35,737
And even though you lowered
Jinzo's attack points,

250
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:38,477
he's still strong enough to
destroy your jet gauntlet.

251
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,100
Here we go again!

252
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,680
My Jinso!

253
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,920
Don't tell me.

254
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,416
That was your special ability, right?

255
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,460
I'm getting a little
tired of this, Robo-boy!

256
